<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Operation Paraquet</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Date/Time:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;24th April,&amp;nbsp;1982 / 22:00:00 Zulu&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Location:&lt;/STRONG&gt; South Atlantic&lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Duration:&lt;/STRONG&gt; 1 Day &lt;BR&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Playable Sides:&lt;/STRONG&gt; United Kingdom&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Taking back the occupied island of South Georgia was the necessary first step in the Royal Navy's campaign to re-take the Falklands. Accordingly, a destroyer group led by HMS Antrim was sent near the island to conduct reconnaissance operations.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On 24 April, the Antrim group was informed that an enemy submarine was operating in the vicinity. This alarming news caused the withdrawal of the group's support vessels to the north, to safer waters.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;During the early morning hours of 25 April, Antrim’s Wessex helicopter&amp;nbsp;spotted a surface contact exiting from Grytviken harbour. What was the Argentinian garrison up to?&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scenario Author: The Stig&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Historical Outcome (SPOILERS)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;EM&gt;ARA Santa Fe, a Balao-class submarine of the Argentine Navy, was spotted as she landed marines as reinforcements to the garrison at Grytviken. &lt;BR&gt;Antrim's Wessex helicopter detected the submarine as she left harbour and attacked her with depth charges; then the Lynx from Brilliant joined in and attacked with torpedos which missed. The next attack was conducted by Endurance's Wasp which engaged with AS.12 missiles, hitting the conning tower and causing major hulll damage. Even so damaged, Santa Fe was nevertheless able to escape and reach the pier at Grytviken, where she was scuttled by her crew.&lt;/EM&gt;</ScenDescription>
